{"seq":20,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-b-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:12:24.969Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"b1358db3a9244dee9466eaf4760542345850ea63895d33c2a645385258953aac","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers that tie to Marrow Fieldworks, plus one that might.\n\n**Named as Marrow Fieldworks:**\n- **PD-5302**: #central-random, Hollis on Oct 14. He called it \"one more ticket number for Marrow Fieldworks,\" for a follow-up from this week, and said no action was needed.\n- **#4409**: Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (Jan 2, 2026). This one is about a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake).\n- **#4412**: the same digest. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n\nOn #4409 and #4412: the digest lists them under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff, but it calls them tickets on \"Pree's dealer account\" rather than naming Marrow Fieldworks outright.\n\n**Might be Marrow Fieldworks:**\n- **#8841**: #central-random, Tobias on Oct 13. It covers West yard Door 2 double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk, at the Plains depots. Hollis called this \"Tobias's dealer account.\" Since Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Jan 5, that's probably the same account, but nobody names it, so I can't confirm.\n\n**Left out because they're other accounts:**\n- FR-882 and PD-4821 are Marrow Agrisupply.\n- #88412 is Tansleigh Packaging.\n\nWhere I looked: both of Moss's Central digests, all of #central-random and #central-team, and this week in #general, #help-it-ops and #inc-tansley-carrier-api. #central-random was the only place with chat from this week, and the three tickets from chat (PD-5302 and #8841) both came from there. I didn't find any Marrow Fieldworks folder in the files you can see."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
